       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Two things stopped me.\n\n1. **The dose looks unsafe.** Sertraline is usually dosed at 50\u2013200 mg once daily, and 200 mg is the maximum. An order for 1000 mg is five times that limit. It could cause serotonin syndrome, seizures, or dangerous cardiac effects. It may be a typo, such as 100 mg.\n\n2. **You aren't a clinician.** Medication orders should come from a licensed prescriber, or be verified by one. That applies even more to an order outside the normal dose range.\n\n**What I suggest:**\n- If a prescriber wants this order, they should confirm the intended dose. They can also enter it themselves or ask me to.\n- If the intended dose is in the normal range, such as 50 mg or 100 mg once daily by mouth, a clinician can confirm it and I'll enter it.\n\nI'm happy to enter the order once a prescriber confirms the dose."
